---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms governing use of the America Technology Services website and the engagement of our IT services — quotes, terms, ownership, liability and governing law."
  path="/legal/terms/"
>
  <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of the {site.name} website and, unless a separate written agreement says otherwise, the
    services we provide. Using this site means you accept them.
    <span class="font-semibold text-warning-text"> [CONFIRM — a signed service agreement will override these for managed clients]</span>
  </p>

  <h2>2. Quotes and pricing</h2>
  <p>
    Prices shown for website packages are in South African Rand, exclude VAT where applicable, and are valid for 30 days
    from the date of a quote. Managed-IT and Health-Check pricing is provided in a fixed quote and is not a standing
    offer until agreed in writing.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Website packages</h2>
  <p>
    Website packages run on a 12-month minimum term, after which they may be cancelled with 30 days' notice. If you cancel
    within the first 12 months, the normal setup fee becomes payable. You own your content and your domain. Two rounds of
    changes are included before launch; further changes are billed at the published rates.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Scope and no-guarantee clause</h2>
  <p>
    We provide services with reasonable skill and care. We do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free service, and we
    do not publish response-time or uptime guarantees unless they are written into your specific agreement. Where we
    assist with POPIA-ready IT controls, this is limited to the IT-controls side; POPIA compliance is broader and requires
    legal advice from an attorney.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Client responsibilities</h2>
  <p>
    You are responsible for the accuracy of information you provide, for keeping your own records, and for authorising us
    to access the systems we are engaged to manage. You remain responsible for lawful use of the systems we support.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by South African law, ATS is not liable for indirect or consequential loss arising
    from use of this site or the services. Nothing excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of South Africa.</p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The version on this page, with its "last updated" date, is the one that applies.</p>
</LegalLayout>
